# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Git lock/temp leftovers (networked mounts have hit lock issues)
*.lock
.git/**/tmp_obj_*

# Secrets / keys (never commit)
API Keys/
*.key
.env

# Local scratch / superseded material
_to_delete/
_verify*.tgz

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDENTIFIED WORKING DATA — do NOT publish. Leading slash = TOP LEVEL ONLY,
# so the pseudonymized release under capsule/data/ is NOT affected.
# The live pipeline (build/ marketing/ analysis/) works over real SEC filings
# keyed by CRD; the public, reproducible dataset is capsule/data/ ONLY.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
/data/
/pilot/
/recon/
/marketing/data/
/marketing/out/
/marketing/__pycache__/
/analysis/out/
/build/out/

# Packaged/scratch archives at the repo root (the capsule ships UNPACKED under capsule/).
# Root-anchored so genuine supplementary archives (frontiers/supplements/*.zip) still ship.
/*.tgz
/*.zip
_*.tgz
_*.zip

# Confidential peer-review correspondence
docs/reviewer_1_report.txt
docs/reviewer_3_report.txt

# LaTeX build products. These are regenerated by frontiers/build_package.sh on every
# run and were being tracked, so every build showed up as a diff.
*.aux
*.blg
*.log
*.out
*.toc
frontiers/manuscript.tex.prefig
# Copied into frontiers/submission/ by build_tracked.sh at build time (lines 21-23).
frontiers/submission/figures/
frontiers/submission/FrontiersinHarvard.cls
frontiers/submission/Frontiers-Harvard.bst
frontiers/submission/references.bib
frontiers/submission/logo*.eps
frontiers/submission/logo*.pdf
frontiers/submission/logos.eps
frontiers/submission/YM-logo.eps

# Identified working data: the two-coder apps embed unredacted brochure passages with real
# firm names, keyed by the same row_id that capsule/data/human_verification/frame.csv maps
# to a fid. Publishing them alongside the capsule would reconstruct the CRD crosswalk the
# article states is withheld. The coder exports and the assignment file carry labels only
# and are safe to ship.
human_validation/*.html

# Reviewer comments are reproduced verbatim in the response letters. The reports themselves
# are already treated as confidential above; these carry the same text. Held back until the
# paper is accepted.
frontiers/submission/response_reviewer_*.txt
frontiers/submission/response_reviewer_*.tex
frontiers/submission/response_reviewer_*.pdf
frontiers/submission/r1_portal.txt
frontiers/submission/r3_portal.txt

# Peer-review correspondence and review-era scaffolding. The paper is published; these
# are the submission package, not the published artifact. They stay on disk and are not
# republished: referee replies and the scripts that built and checked them, tracked-changes
# copies, the version that was submitted, and the packaging notes that name the referees.
frontiers/submission/build_responses.py
frontiers/submission/build_tracked.sh
frontiers/submission/fix_tracked.py
frontiers/submission/verify_response_refs.py
frontiers/submission/verify_letter_structure.py
frontiers/submission/manuscript_tracked.*
frontiers/submission/manuscript_v1_as_submitted.*
frontiers/submission/references_v1_as_submitted.bib
frontiers/submission/README_package.md
frontiers/submission/SUBMISSION_README.md
frontiers/submission/*_portal.txt
frontiers/submission/response_reviewer_*
